### Correction and publication behavior

Inspection confirms that metadata lengths are charged with checked arithmetic before owned copies or qualified-owner construction, and one budget is passed across the whole selection. Each method-owner copy consumes that budget. The expanded class-header span is checked before annotation copies, owner construction and header allocation. The bounded JSON writer rejects an excessive write before requesting capacity or extending the buffer and accounts for the trailing newline. Generation propagates these errors before publication staging.

The rejected synthetic output and invalid-provenance output are absent. No publication staging remains in either output parent. The existing 301,972-byte declaration output still has SHA-256 `81df6c8d6eb0d167d89410f898d7de8d9279ee175fbd637a1ca68bb2dc0ed88f`. The runner asserts byte preservation after normal checking, replacement refusal and stress checking. The retained deliberately changed file is exactly the original bytes plus its known suffix and is rejected by checking. These observations support the bounded failure and preservation behavior for the recorded flows.

